.TH AMERIKA-BOOT 1 "2026-10-21" "Amerika OS" "Amerika OS Manual"
.SH NAME
amerika\-boot \- switch the Amerika OS boot screen on or off
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B amerika\-boot
.RB { status | enable | disable }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B amerika\-boot
selects the Plymouth boot and shutdown theme installed by the
.B amerika\-boot
package. Installing the package registers the theme as an alternative of
.I default.plymouth
at a low priority and does not select it. Only
.B enable
selects it and rebuilds the initial RAM disk with
.BR update\-initramfs (8);
if the rebuild fails the previous selection is restored.
.PP
The command never edits GRUB, the kernel command line, the EFI System Partition or the disk layout.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Print whether the Amerika theme is the active one, as JSON.
.TP
.B enable
Select the Amerika theme. It appears at the next start.
.TP
.B disable
Restore the previous theme (or the automatic choice).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/plymouth/themes/amerika
The theme.
.TP
.I /var/lib/amerika\-os/boot/previous.json
The theme to restore.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amerika\-login (1),
.BR amerika\-flavour (7),
.BR plymouthd (8)
